---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Chunking Strategy Ablation | Ravikumar Buragapu"
			description="A controlled comparison of fixed, recursive, sentence-window, and semantic chunking for retrieval-augmented QA."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<p>RAG RESEARCH · RETRIEVAL · CONTROLLED ABLATION</p>
			<h1>Chunking Strategy Ablation</h1>
			<p>
				Is fixed-size chunking really the best default? Compare
				fixed, recursive, sentence-window, and semantic strategies
				with one corpus, one TF-IDF embedder, 50 hand-written
				questions, and fixed retrieval depth k=5.
			</p>

			<section aria-labelledby="measures">
				<h2 id="measures">Measure retrieval quality against context cost</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>Recall@5 against explicit gold evidence sentences.</li>
					<li>Answer exact match, optional LLM-judge score, and editable human review.</li>
					<li>cl100k context tokens, retrieval and end-to-end latency, and configurable token cost.</li>
					<li>Identical corpus, embedder, question set, answerer, and retrieval depth across chunkers.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					The bundled engineering corpus is original illustrative
					fixture text, not private papers or domain guidance.
					Local extractive mode makes no provider calls; LLM mode
					is optional and requires an approved endpoint.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="run">
				<h2 id="run">Run the benchmark</h2>
				<pre><code>cd chunking-ablation
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
chunking-ablation
pytest</code></pre>
				<p>
					<a href="https://github.com/buragapuravi/my_research_work/tree/main/chunking-ablation"
						>Read the project README</a
					>
					·
					<a href="/projects/research-chat">Explore Chat with My Research</a>
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
